            "result_text": "I'll help you set up a git server with automatic deployment to a web server. Here's the configuration:\n\n## Server Setup\n\n**1. Create the bare git repository:**\n```bash\nmkdir -p /git/server\ncd /git/server\ngit init --bare\n```\n\n**2. Create the web root directory:**\n```bash\nmkdir -p /var/www/html\n```\n\n**3. Set up the post-receive hook** (this auto-deploys on push):\n\nCreate `/git/server/hooks/post-receive` with:\n```bash\n#!/bin/bash\nGIT_WORK_TREE=/var/www/html git checkout -f\n```\n\nMake it executable:\n```bash\nchmod +x /git/server/hooks/post-receive\n```\n\n**4. Initialize the web directory** (so first checkout works):\n```bash\ncd /var/www/html\ngit init\ngit remote add origin /git/server\ngit fetch origin\ngit checkout -b master origin/master 2>/dev/null || true\n```\n\n**5. Set up a web server on port 8080**\n\nUsing Python (simplest for testing):\n```bash\ncd /var/www/html\npython3 -m http.server 8080\n```\n\nOr with nginx, create `/etc/nginx/sites-available/default`:\n```nginx\nserver {\n    listen 8080;\n    root /var/www/html;\n    index index.html;\n}\n```\n\nThen restart: `sudo systemctl restart nginx`\n\n## Client Usage\n\nFrom your local machine:\n```bash\ngit clone user@server:/git/server my-repo\ncd my-repo\necho \"hello world\" > hello.html\ngit add hello.html\ngit commit -m \"add hello.html\"\ngit push origin master\n```\n\nThen test:\n```bash\ncurl http://server:8080/hello.html\n# Output: hello world\n```\n\nThe post-receive hook automatically checks out the pushed code to `/var/www/html`, so it appears on the web server immediately."
